## 🛠️ Technologies Used

### HTML5
Provides the semantic structure of the application, including navigation, sections, tables, forms, dialogs, and dashboard components.

### CSS3
Used for styling, layouts, dashboard cards, responsive behavior, themes, tables, modals, and visual effects.

The HTML references an external stylesheet named `style.css`.

### JavaScript
Provides the application behavior, including navigation, form handling, filtering, modal controls, notifications, theme changes, report generation, and export actions.

The HTML references an external script named `script.js`.

### Chart.js
Used for creating data visualizations through HTML canvas elements.

Charts represented in the HTML include:

- Overview performance trend.
- Performance distribution.
- Department comparison.
- Attendance presence pulse.

### jsPDF
A JavaScript library included for generating PDF documents in the browser.

### Font Awesome
Provides icons for navigation, buttons, KPI cards, notifications, attendance indicators, and other interface elements.

### Google Fonts — Inter
The Inter typeface is loaded to provide consistent typography.

### Netlify
The live application is hosted at:

https://analyticsdashb.netlify.app/

The hosting configuration should be checked in the repository to confirm the deployment workflow.

