## 📁 Project Structure

The basic project structure referenced by the HTML is:

```text
PulseAnalytics/
│
├── index.html
├── style.css
├── script.js
├── README.md
└── assets/
    └── (optional images, icons, or other local assets)
```

### File Descriptions

**`index.html`**

Contains the dashboard structure, sidebar navigation, header, seven application modules, tables, forms, modal dialogs, and external library references.

**`style.css`**

Contains the visual styling, responsive layouts, dashboard components, modal appearance, themes, and other presentation rules.

**`script.js`**

Contains the JavaScript application logic. The HTML references an `app` object for actions such as navigation, modal handling, employee and goal forms, attendance filtering, notifications, and data exports.

**`README.md`**

Documents the project, features, technologies, setup, usage, and future development plans.

**`assets/`**

An optional directory for local images, logos, screenshots, and other static resources.

> The HTML references `style.css` and `script.js`. Confirm that these files exist in the repository and that their names and paths match exactly.

