## 💾 Data and Storage

The HTML provides the interface for entering, displaying, and exporting employee, goal, attendance, and report information.

However, the HTML alone does not establish how data is stored.

Depending on the implementation in `script.js`, the application may use in-memory data, browser storage, or a connected backend.

### Browser Storage
If browser storage is implemented, data may remain available in the same browser after a refresh. Browser-local storage does not automatically synchronize records between different users or devices.

### Backend Integration
A production system can connect the dashboard to an API and database to support centralized records, authentication, permissions, and multi-user access.

### Recommended Production Architecture

```text
User Interface
      |
      v
HTML + CSS + JavaScript
      |
      v
Authenticated Backend API
      |
      v
Database
      |
      +---- Employee Records
      +---- Department Records
      +---- Goals and KPIs
      +---- Attendance Logs
      +---- Report Definitions
```

This architecture is a recommendation for future integration, not a claim that the current frontend already includes these services.

